    "progress_bound": "Nonreused token IDs use checked allocation. Namespace/endpoint admission is fenced and caller threads quiescent. Each extra rescan follows actual deletion, never a still-present busy selection. No new timer/wait loop or readiness contract.",
    "ownership": "Same captured root/generation, original charges, authority and backing owners. Missing selected token is no whole-namespace/physical/root cleanup proof. Existing authority/memory/zero-lease/sealing/invalidation requirements remain. No new root/pin/registry/family/custody or IRQ change; C02 updated.",
    "fixture_boundary": "Production passes an empty generic hook. Serialized kernel controls execute actual peer close after selection with IPC/lifecycle/table guards released. Raw capability selectors stay at documented kernel ABI fixture boundary; no userspace owner exception.",
    "failure_policy": "Existing five-second reclamation deadline unchanged. Every live/abandoned claim remains fenced. Rejected physical cleanup is never reconstructed or resubmitted. Supervisor helper still uses bounded timer polling; root-wait notification/progress qualification remains open."
  },
